  message: "DONE in PR #2329 for 11 of the 15 rows; the other 4 cannot be fixed by the key and are filed as their own item. What each analyzer emits was read off a run of a fixture (one file per language), not off the item.\nRE-KEYED: Rust x2 and C# x4 to annotation: (rust.py and csharp.py write meta.annotations; the Rust rows also take a runtime's path, tokio::test). WGSL x3 to meta_match on meta.entry_point. Laravel x2 to base_class ShouldQueue plus the directory (Jobs/ for task, Listeners/ for event_handler): keyed on the interface alone both rows would have stamped both concepts on every queued class.\nCANNOT BE FIXED BY THE KEY (each marked CANNOT FIRE in its YAML, pinned by a test as not matching): PHP @test docblock and #[Test] attribute (php.py records neither), F# attributes, D @(\"test\"), Plug's conn.\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (dev a5b3cca93 vs the branch, 2026-11-22): the item's own repro, a C# [Fact] method and a Rust #[test] fn, on a fixture: both carry test_function now, none did on dev. Real code: bincode +80 test_function; microservices-demo +3 (C# [Fact]); koel +9 event_handler (queued listeners) and +1 task (queued job). No stable id moved on any of 19 trees. The row tests were red before the rows changed.\nFOUND BESIDE IT, SAME CAUSE (a row keyed on a shape the analyzer does not emit): 18 rows anchor a method name at its start, and the Python, Ruby, Swift, Scala, Groovy and PHP analyzers name a method Class.method, so a Python test method in a class is not a test_function and Falcon responders are not route handlers. Only PHP's row was repaired here (it reads the last segment), and then restricted to *Test.php files after it stamped 5 production testSetup methods on koel. The other 17 are filed as their own item: they change test and route detection in five languages.\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/three_pr_plan_11222026/pr2/RESULTS.md.\n\nFILED FROM THIS: WI-rasok (the 17 method-name rows), WI-somog (the four rows the key cannot fix)."  # eba6
